@page "/about"

<PageTitle>Legendary — About</PageTitle>

<div class="about">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <section class="panel panel--disclaimer">
        <h2 class="panel__title">Unofficial fan app</h2>
        <p>
            This is an <strong>unofficial, fan-made</strong> companion tool. It is not produced,
            endorsed, licensed, or affiliated with the publishers or rights holders of
            <em>Legendary: A Marvel Deck Building Game</em>, Marvel, or any related company.
        </p>
        <p>
            All game, character, and set names are trademarks of their respective owners and are
            referenced here purely to help owners of the physical game set it up faster. This app
            ships <strong>no card text, art, or copyrighted game content</strong> — only the names
            needed to randomise a legal setup, and the public setup rules.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">You must own the physical game to play.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2 class="panel__title">Setup rules used</h2>
        <p class="muted">Per-player base counts the randomiser follows:</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="rules">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Players</th><th>Heroes</th><th>Villains</th><th>Henchmen</th><th>Strikes</th><th>Bystanders</th><th>Twists*</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var r in SetupTable.ByPlayers.Values.OrderBy(r => r.Players))
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <td>@r.Players</td>
                            <td>@r.Heroes</td>
                            <td>@r.VillainGroups</td>
                            <td>@r.Henchmen</td>
                            <td>@r.MasterStrikes</td>
                            <td>@r.Bystanders</td>
                            <td>@r.SchemeTwists</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="muted small">*Base and Dark City Schemes run an 8-Twist track (Twist 1…8 → “Evil Wins”), so a standard game uses 8. Solo play and a few Schemes change this — the Scheme card is always authoritative.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="notes">
            <li>Each Mastermind's <strong>Always Leads</strong> group is forced into the setup and marked <span class="badge">Required</span>.</li>
            <li>Master Strikes, Bystanders and Scheme Twists are shown on the Mastermind, Villains and Scheme cards respectively.</li>
            <li>Any Scheme with special setup or Twist rules shows a reminder to read its card — see below for why the full text isn't reproduced here.</li>
            <li>2–5 player counts follow the rulebook; the 1-player column uses the published solo variant.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2 class="panel__title">Why no full card text or rulebook?</h2>
        <p>
            Card names, the number of each card type per player count, and which group a Mastermind
            “Always Leads” are short facts — this tool uses those to build a legal setup.
        </p>
        <p>
            The <em>wording</em> of card abilities and the rulebook, however, is creative writing owned
            by the game's publisher and Marvel. Reproducing it in full — even reworded — would copy
            copyrighted content, so this app intentionally leaves it out and points you to your cards
            instead. Fan wikis that host full text do so at the rights holders' discretion, not under a
            licence this app shares.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">Short version: setup facts are fine to include; full card/rules text isn't, so it's kept out.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2 class="panel__title">How rerolls work</h2>
        <p class="muted">
            Each category can be rerolled on its own while everything else stays put. After any
            reroll the app re-checks the Mastermind's required group and keeps it in play.
        </p>
    </section>

    <p class="version muted small">Legendary Companion · PWA · works offline once loaded.</p>
</div>
